title: It already exists, it's just regular money
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Hot take, from a voice memo (Sep 13, 2026).

I just overheard these guys lamenting how all of the payment services were owned by somebody, and that they didn't have any way to pay each other without some capitalist intermediary that either extracted data or additional money from them. They were trying to figure out how they would invent this. And my head was just screaming: it already exists, it's just regular money!

Right? You just pay each other with dollars. And you can get the dollars out. Technically, you need a bank to do that, I guess. But the bank doesn't extract a fee to do your transaction once you have the money. Oh, my God.

Governments make money so that citizens of that government can just hand each other money, and agree that it's worth something because the government is supporting it, not just some company, right?

That might need a little bit more economic theory.

